omising a strong story you're going  to laugh you're going to cry you're  going to have all the feels is what i  would say well said  we thought our joys would be an ending  the new show the rings of power is a  prequel to the oscar-winning movies it's  set thousands of years prior it's  actually based on a series of appendices  from lord of the rings not a standalone  tolkien book but it has fans and that's  why amazon is shelling out so much money  it's trying to create a franchise to  anchor amazon prime video subscribers  much in the same way competing streaming  service disney plus takes advantage of  its popular franchises if you're a star  wars fan if if you're a marvel fan you  can't go anywhere this is you've got to  have this service  now attracting and holding onto  subscribers is only part of the story  most amazon prime video subscribers get  their memberships as a throw in for  signing up for amazon prime's delivery  service streaming is about keeping those  200 million customers happy and spending  prime members spend a lot of money in  amazon store  other streaming services also work to  monetize subscribers in other ways  netflix is moving into gaming  disney's doing it with amusement parks  over the summer it's been letting  subscribers in early and offering  substantially discounted tickets so that  means the disney plus subscriber who's  worth let's say seventy dollars a year  uh is now worth thousands of dollars a  year to just  now the biggest part of amazon's  business is retail well its biggest  retail competitor is getting into  streaming walmart announced a deal  earlier this month where people who sign  up for its online delivery service  will get paramount plus for free mike  armstrong global news  competitive swimming's governing body  has approved the use of a specialized  swim cap designed for afro hair  the covering was banned from last year's  olympics in part because the  international swimming federation  reportedly said the caps did not fit the  natural form of the head many swimmers  criticized the comments sparking a  review which concluded that there was no  advantage to be gained from using them  soul cap a company that sells the caps  called the decision a huge step forward  toward improving inclusion in the sport  today marks the 50th anniversary of an  event that definitively changed canada's  biggest sport the 1972 summit series was  billed as a bitter battle on the ice  team canada facing off against the  soviet union in an eight-game roller  coaster that captured the fascination of  millions but for many it was more than  just hockey decades later the game's  legacy can still be felt eric sorenson  looks back at the iconic battle on and  off the ice  the 72 summit series is steeped in  hockey lore canada and the soviet union  the seminal matchup of the two great  hockey powers and the iconic players on  both teams in this country it was an  opportunity to affirm canada's hockey  supremacy against the backdrop of the  cold war  back then we didn't know a lot about the  soviets they were this scary image it  became  more than just one hockey team trying to  beat the other it was proving that our  system was better than our their system  for decades canada did reign supreme at  the olympics and in the amateur hockey  world but by the 1960s the soviet union  dominated their best could play while  canadian professionals weren't allowed  so this series was our chance finally to  prove our best were the best  scoring in the opening seconds canada  looked unstoppable i think we had a  smugness with goals quickly by esposito  and that it just seemed like you know  canada was vindicated we were the hockey  capital of the world what happened next  would change how the sport itself was  viewed the soviets stormed back to take  charge of the game and the series in  vancouver canadian fans booed their  heroes  canada of course with grit and  determination proved their mettle when  the series moved to moscow  they were playing for their country now  and a huge amount of pride as hockey  players and as canadians was on the line  so i think that might be the greatest  thing about the canadian team is it  showed resiliency and it showed the  ability to come back um from from  something where they you know look to be  a national disaster but what the summit  revealed was that international hockey  was indeed worthy competition it changed  and there was more respect for the  international players the north american  game itself got better with the infusion  of russians and others europeans were  welcomed to the nhl  eventually the iron curtain came down  and so the  hockey world became a much bigger and  open place as a result of that series  september 1972 was a roller coaster of  emotions for hockey fans  and without giving away the ending the  summit series did show that canadian  hockey at times can be the best in the  world eric sorensen global news toronto  what a triumph for our country that's  global national for this friday night  i'm farah nasser and on behalf of our  whole crew here i want to thank you so  much for spending part of your evening  with us  tonight's york canada is the sunset in  point o barrel ontario courtesy of  global's own calling christy who by the  way is going to be at the anchor desk  tomorrow we love seeing your canada so  please keep emailing us your photos at  viewers  globalnational.com until friday take  care of yourselves and each other have a  wonderful and safe weekend good night  [Music]
 

